<!DOCTYPE reference
  PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="metadata_document_properties_field_codes" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Metadata - Document Properties/Field Codes</title>
   <abstract>This section covers document properties and field codes in DOCX — the metadata fields
      that identify, attribute, and classify a document independently of its body content — and one
      scenario: document properties populated in the file's properties panel and mapped during
      conversion. The converter reads each populated property and maps it to the corresponding DITA
         <codeph>&lt;prolog&gt;</codeph> element, making the document's authorship, dates, and
      classification data available to downstream publishing and search tools.</abstract>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>document</keyword>
        <keyword>properties</keyword>
        <keyword>property</keyword>
        <keyword>field</keyword>
        <keyword>Field</keyword>
        <keyword>content</keyword>
        <indexterm>document</indexterm>
        <indexterm>properties</indexterm>
        <indexterm>property</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d635e7">
         <p>
            <b>Metadata</b> is structured information about a document, separate from its body content. It records attributes such as authorship, creation and revision dates, and classification tags. This information is what allows downstream publishing systems, content management platforms, and search indexes to reliably identify, track, and retrieve the document.</p>
         <p>In a .docx file, this information lives in two places: <b>document properties</b>, set
            once for the entire file through File → Info → Properties, and <b>field codes</b>, which
            display those property values as visible text in the body or cover page (inserted via
            Insert → Quick Parts → Field Codes). A field code always shows the same value as its
            source property, even if referenced in multiple places like the header, footer, or cover
            page.</p>
         <p>The following properties and their equivalent field codes are recognized and extracted
            during conversion:</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Document properties and field codes</title>
            <tgroup cols="3">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <colspec colname="c3"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>Property</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>Field Code</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>Description</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Title</entry>
                     <entry>TITLE</entry>
                     <entry>The controlled publication name of the document</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Author</entry>
                     <entry>AUTHOR</entry>
                     <entry>The person responsible for the content</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Company</entry>
                     <entry>COMPANY</entry>
                     <entry>The organisation that owns the document</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Subject</entry>
                     <entry>SUBJECT</entry>
                     <entry>The topic or system the document covers</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Keywords</entry>
                     <entry>KEYWORDS</entry>
                     <entry>Terms used to index and classify the document</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Version / Revision number</entry>
                     <entry>REVNUM</entry>
                     <entry>The release or draft number</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Created date</entry>
                     <entry>CREATEDATE</entry>
                     <entry>The date the document was first created</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Last modified date</entry>
                     <entry>SAVEDATE</entry>
                     <entry>The date the document was last saved</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Status</entry>
                     <entry>—</entry>
                     <entry>The review or approval state of the document</entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Custom property</entry>
                     <entry>DOCPROPERTY [name]</entry>
                     <entry>The value of any named custom property</entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p>The converter reads the properties package at the start of each conversion run and maps each populated property to the corresponding DITA element:</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Metadata fields mapped to DITA</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="1*"/>
               <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="1.2*"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>.docx Property / Field Code</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Author</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;prolog&gt;&lt;author&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Created date</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;prolog&gt;&lt;critdates&gt;&lt;created&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Last Modified date</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;prolog&gt;&lt;critdates&gt;&lt;revised&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Keywords</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;metadata&gt;&lt;keywords&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Company</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;othermeta name="company"&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Status</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;othermeta name="status"&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Category</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;othermeta name="category"&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Title</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;title&gt; or &lt;mainbooktitle&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <entry>Subject</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeph>&lt;othermeta name="subject"&gt;</codeph>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <note type="important">A blank property produces an incomplete
               <codeph>&lt;prolog&gt;</codeph> for that field. The converter does not infer a value
            from body content. Populate document properties before submission to eliminate manual
            metadata entry in Oxygen XML or another DITA editor after conversion.</note>
      </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
